Z||000000||86seyellow||08-05-2001||10:34 AM||||ok, here is one for all of you.<P>Car has been purring , the best it ever has. let it idle one day as I am polishing it. it died all of a sudden like someone turned it off. SO i go out and by a new distributor , ignition module, pickup coil and coil. put it all in and I find that it is idling really low. so I figure I put distributor a little ahead of where she was. Well I set it back a little and it started, ran great, but I didnt tightn the distributor down so I had to turn her off so it wouldnt leak alot of oil. I tighten the dist down. go back into car and try to start, nothing , it cranks but no go. I figure I flooded it. SO i let it sit and all of a sudden I hear the starter clicjkoing now. Wont crank. so Is the starte screwed now?? this is a 86 yellow se with a 2,8 in it. New wires, plugs rotor, cap, dist , ignition module. coil and all. even a new battery, help me plaese<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-05-2001||12:08 PM||||I know you said that you have a new battery .But I would think that the battery has been drained. If you dont have any meters turn your headlights on and look at them, while somebody else sits in the car and cranks it. If the lights get very dim while cranking it you have a battery that needs to be recharged. the other problem you have...well it seems that you have it figured out,although from what you describe I am not sure I would have come to the same conclusion as you did by changeing the dist. and electronics that go with it.but we learn something new every day.hope this helps you||||reg||1
